  [1mRoot cause:[0m [38;5;153mgetDiscountRate[39m returned [38;5;153mundefined[39m for any code not in [38;5;153mRATES[39m. [38;5;153mfinalPrice[39m then computed [38;5;153mprice - price * [39m
  [38;5;153mundefined[39m, and arithmetic on [38;5;153mundefined[39m yields [38;5;153mNaN[39m. The bad value originated in the lookup, so that's where I fixed it
  — returning [38;5;153m0[39m ("no discount") instead of [38;5;153mundefined[39m, rather than patching the arithmetic in [38;5;153mfinalPrice[39m.

  [1mVerification[0m — your original command now prints the expected value:

